  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "The fixed background target is the literal finite product gamma_n=Measure.pi (fun i:Fin n => gaussianReal 0 1), a real signed f, Phi(s)=s*Real.log s, and D_i f(x)=fderiv R f x(Pi.single i 1). Entropy is homogeneous: integral Phi(f^2)-Phi(integral f^2). Printed FIRST4.6 concerns the normalized standardized RGO law r_y against standard Gaussian, not this standalone product function theorem.",
    "domains": "Every natural n including zero, canonical real finite Pi Borel space; f globally C2 and compactly supported. Function square, Phi(square), every coordinate derivative square and their finite sum must genuinely be L1. Domains are conclusions/internal analytic obligations rather than public supplied certificates. Signed functions, zeros and zero mass are allowed with totalized log and Phi(0)=0.",
    "quantifiers": "For all n and real f, C2 and compact support imply all four L1 clauses and one homogeneous entropy inequality. Internal slice estimates use every fixed original complementary coordinate; the proof may not add a marginal square-root differentiability premise or prechosen inequality witness.",
    "assumptions": "Only n/f plus C2 and compact support occur at the sealed compact interface. Compact C2 is an explicit authored sufficient background class narrower than the pinned external W12 Gaussian product theorem. The external theorem separately consumes actual L2 of g and each partial, differentiability, continuous partials and Phi(g^2) L1. These may be derived from compact C2, never supplied anew as public certificates. No positivity, normalized f^2, bound, coordinate LSI, law or domain premise is permitted.",
    "conclusion": "Ent_gamma_n(f^2) <= 2* integral sum_i (D_i f)^2, plus genuine integrability of f^2, Phi(f^2), each derivative square and the full sum. It is a finite-product compact analytic background result, not the printed Wasserstein/Fisher conclusion, full Hilbert Gaussian LSI or noncompact square-root density LSI.",
    "scopes": "SPHMC v1 S4.E6 FIRST inequality and S4.SS1.p4.3 invoke Gaussian log-Sobolev together with Talagrand and omit tensorization proof. External SLT TensorizedGLSI gives entropy_subadditive then a separate coordinate-energy bound. Authored original-slice induction through actual bounded binary entropy39 and scalar compact LSI38 is a different sufficient OR route; no RMS-marginal derivative route or source attribution to that authored proof is justified.",
    "constant_dependencies": "Each scalar variance is exactly one; function-LSI coefficient is exactly 2, independent of n. Coordinate energy is the literal finite sum of squared directional derivatives, not the squared operator norm of fderiv under the default Pi sup norm. Fin0 is the actual singleton probability law: entropy zero and empty energy zero without forcing f value zero. A future sqrt-density application uses energy I/4 only after noncompact/Hilbert/coherent-law adapters; T2 and W2 remain separate."
  },
